\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Master table: every codec run.} Generated from each run's own JSON by \texttt  {ml/make\_table.py}, not transcribed. Run-name grammar (\texttt  {f4r2}, \texttt  {monthblock}, \dots  ) is decoded in \S  \ref {sec:inputdata}. \textbf  {There are two read-out columns and they are not interchangeable.} $^\S  $\emph  {Pooled ridge} is \texttt  {probe\_kfold}'s ridge on the \emph  {section-mean} embedding. It is the comparability bridge across this whole archive and it is never a verdict: geostrophic transport at $26.5^\circ $N is the east--west contrast \emph  {across} the section, and a section mean is precisely the statistic in which that contrast cancels --- measured on the anchor's own embeddings, $z$ along the section correlates $r=0.99$ at one cell, $0.88$ at five and $0.35$ at eighty, so the mean averages about \textbf  {2.5 effective independent pixels of 265}. $^\P  $\textbf  {Unpooled head} is \texttt  {probe\_head}'s attention query over the section's \emph  {individual} pixels (\S  \ref {sec:ladder}) --- the verdict column. It is mostly empty because the flag that produces it defaulted to off until 2026-08-21: it exists in \textbf  {12 of 204} archived bundles. \textbf  {A dash means not measured and is never a copied pooled number}; the missing rows are being filled by eval-only ladders over the already-published checkpoints, which retrain nothing. \textbf  {Each column has its own bar and they must not be crossed.} The pooled bar is the wind-stress-only \emph  {ridge}: $r=0.531$ on the $1^\circ $ tensors, $0.568$ on the quarter-degree, $0.670$ at pentad and $0.607$ at daily, all on the same folds. The unpooled bar is the same head fed wind stress with nothing pooled, and where it has been measured --- the pentad section --- it reads $0.690$; there is no unpooled wind bar on the monthly section. The matched raw-data controls, the head fed section values instead of embeddings, are $0.659$ ($1^\circ $ deep, $3\times 3$), $0.628$ (quarter-degree monthly) and $0.693$ (pentad). \textbf  {Read the pentad row against those and the codec loses}: run-415's own head ($0.659$) sits below both its raw-$3\times 3$ control ($0.693$) and the unpooled wind bar ($0.690$), where its pooled figure ($0.637$) merely sat below a pooled bar. Sample sizes differ by cadence --- 240 monthly transport labels, 1{,}459 pentad, 7{,}290 daily --- so a CI in the bottom block is not comparable with one above it, and neither is a point estimate. $^\dagger $chan\% is comparable only within one channel set (its persistence baseline moves with the channels). Dip = share of the winter 2009--10 collapse amplitude captured out-of-fold. $^\ast $global14b is an exact-configuration replication on a different runner: codec-seed noise on the pooled k-fold is $\approx \pm 0.05$, which the four pixel24/patch24 rows (0.515--0.585 across 30k--60k steps) are consistent with, and patch24-1M is flat from the first probe to the millionth step (\S  \ref {sec:limits}). The two patch24 rows are a codec-seed pair and are why no single-seed number in either read-out column is a level: pooled moves $0.012$ between them, unpooled $0.036$. $^\ddagger $in-training probe at the final step. Stage-2 figures for global14b and global15sst are \emph  {withdrawn}: a poisoned embedding cache (\S  \ref {sec:limits}). $^\parallel $The month-block codec has neither number: no probe bundle was archived for it, its probe path is block-shaped, and it is JAX/TPU-trained and so never pooled with a PyTorch number (\S  \ref {sec:jax}). Its evidence is \S  \ref {sec:block}'s reconstruction audit. Codecs still training or not yet dispatched carry no number at all and are Table~\ref {tab:inflight}.}}{14}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:master}{{4}{14}{\textbf {Master table: every codec run.} Generated from each run's own JSON by \texttt {ml/make\_table.py}, not transcribed. Run-name grammar (\texttt {f4r2}, \texttt {monthblock}, \dots ) is decoded in \S \ref {sec:inputdata}. \textbf {There are two read-out columns and they are not interchangeable.} $^\S $\emph {Pooled ridge} is \texttt {probe\_kfold}'s ridge on the \emph {section-mean} embedding. It is the comparability bridge across this whole archive and it is never a verdict: geostrophic transport at $26.5^\circ $N is the east--west contrast \emph {across} the section, and a section mean is precisely the statistic in which that contrast cancels --- measured on the anchor's own embeddings, $z$ along the section correlates $r=0.99$ at one cell, $0.88$ at five and $0.35$ at eighty, so the mean averages about \textbf {2.5 effective independent pixels of 265}. $^\P $\textbf {Unpooled head} is \texttt {probe\_head}'s attention query over the section's \emph {individual} pixels (\S \ref {sec:ladder}) --- the verdict column. It is mostly empty because the flag that produces it defaulted to off until 2026-08-21: it exists in \textbf {12 of 204} archived bundles. \textbf {A dash means not measured and is never a copied pooled number}; the missing rows are being filled by eval-only ladders over the already-published checkpoints, which retrain nothing. \textbf {Each column has its own bar and they must not be crossed.} The pooled bar is the wind-stress-only \emph {ridge}: $r=0.531$ on the $1^\circ $ tensors, $0.568$ on the quarter-degree, $0.670$ at pentad and $0.607$ at daily, all on the same folds. The unpooled bar is the same head fed wind stress with nothing pooled, and where it has been measured --- the pentad section --- it reads $0.690$; there is no unpooled wind bar on the monthly section. The matched raw-data controls, the head fed section values instead of embeddings, are $0.659$ ($1^\circ $ deep, $3\times 3$), $0.628$ (quarter-degree monthly) and $0.693$ (pentad). \textbf {Read the pentad row against those and the codec loses}: run-415's own head ($0.659$) sits below both its raw-$3\times 3$ control ($0.693$) and the unpooled wind bar ($0.690$), where its pooled figure ($0.637$) merely sat below a pooled bar. Sample sizes differ by cadence --- 240 monthly transport labels, 1{,}459 pentad, 7{,}290 daily --- so a CI in the bottom block is not comparable with one above it, and neither is a point estimate. $^\dagger $chan\% is comparable only within one channel set (its persistence baseline moves with the channels). Dip = share of the winter 2009--10 collapse amplitude captured out-of-fold. $^\ast $global14b is an exact-configuration replication on a different runner: codec-seed noise on the pooled k-fold is $\approx \pm 0.05$, which the four pixel24/patch24 rows (0.515--0.585 across 30k--60k steps) are consistent with, and patch24-1M is flat from the first probe to the millionth step (\S \ref {sec:limits}). The two patch24 rows are a codec-seed pair and are why no single-seed number in either read-out column is a level: pooled moves $0.012$ between them, unpooled $0.036$. $^\ddagger $in-training probe at the final step. Stage-2 figures for global14b and global15sst are \emph {withdrawn}: a poisoned embedding cache (\S \ref {sec:limits}). $^\parallel $The month-block codec has neither number: no probe bundle was archived for it, its probe path is block-shaped, and it is JAX/TPU-trained and so never pooled with a PyTorch number (\S \ref {sec:jax}). Its evidence is \S \ref {sec:block}'s reconstruction audit. Codecs still training or not yet dispatched carry no number at all and are Table~\ref {tab:inflight}}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Bottleneck width $d_z$ versus its two customers, on the 12-channel North-Atlantic tensor at matched training steps. Field prediction (top) saturates by $d_z{=}16$--$32$; the AMOC probe (bottom, with 95\% block-bootstrap CIs) rises to a peak at $d_z{=}64$ and turns over at 128 --- 128 ridge features against $\sim $220 truth months per fold overfits. $d_z{=}64$ became the working setting, a choice made when the tensor had 12 channels.}}{15}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dz}{{1}{15}{Bottleneck width $d_z$ versus its two customers, on the 12-channel North-Atlantic tensor at matched training steps. Field prediction (top) saturates by $d_z{=}16$--$32$; the AMOC probe (bottom, with 95\% block-bootstrap CIs) rises to a peak at $d_z{=}64$ and turns over at 128 --- 128 ridge features against $\sim $220 truth months per fold overfits. $d_z{=}64$ became the working setting, a choice made when the tensor had 12 channels}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Year-blocked k-fold correlation with monthly deseasonalized RAPID transport, all codec generations, 95\% CIs. Adding wind stress (orange) nearly doubled the defensible probe; training globally cost the Atlantic read-out nothing. The deep-tensor codecs (green) fall back onto the dashed wind-only baseline --- a ridge on section-mean wind stress with no embedding at all.}}{15}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kfold}{{2}{15}{Year-blocked k-fold correlation with monthly deseasonalized RAPID transport, all codec generations, 95\% CIs. Adding wind stress (orange) nearly doubled the defensible probe; training globally cost the Atlantic read-out nothing. The deep-tensor codecs (green) fall back onto the dashed wind-only baseline --- a ridge on section-mean wind stress with no embedding at all}{figure.2}{}}
