\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Left: the cadence ladder.} One-step forecast ratio against step size, holding everything else fixed --- same frozen pentad codec, same embeddings, same $1024\times 16$ head with input noise, same pixels, 20{,}000 steps, each arm scored against its own persistence baseline. The two points at 30 days are the Argo-carrying and Argo-free bin selections. Smooth and monotone --- but $K{=}24$ is fixed, so context span co-varies with the step, and \S  \ref {sec:factorial} shows the span is what this curve is measuring. \textbf  {Right: the component ladder at 5 days}, one variable per arm against the two-seed control (dotted). Rescaling the exposure-bias noise to the pentad embedding scale is catastrophic, removing the Argo targets makes training \emph  {worse}, a continuous season phase changes nothing, and only restricting the head's inputs to an 8-level-per-dimension alphabet beats the control. Every arm is $n{=}1$ except the control, so these are directions; the control pair's own $|\Delta |$ is $0.0011$.}}{34}{figure.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cadence}{{11}{34}{\textbf {Left: the cadence ladder.} One-step forecast ratio against step size, holding everything else fixed --- same frozen pentad codec, same embeddings, same $1024\times 16$ head with input noise, same pixels, 20{,}000 steps, each arm scored against its own persistence baseline. The two points at 30 days are the Argo-carrying and Argo-free bin selections. Smooth and monotone --- but $K{=}24$ is fixed, so context span co-varies with the step, and \S \ref {sec:factorial} shows the span is what this curve is measuring. \textbf {Right: the component ladder at 5 days}, one variable per arm against the two-seed control (dotted). Rescaling the exposure-bias noise to the pentad embedding scale is catastrophic, removing the Argo targets makes training \emph {worse}, a continuous season phase changes nothing, and only restricting the head's inputs to an 8-level-per-dimension alphabet beats the control. Every arm is $n{=}1$ except the control, so these are directions; the control pair's own $|\Delta |$ is $0.0011$}{figure.11}{}}
