\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {What each codec's round trip loses}, at full visibility --- encode and decode with nothing masked and nothing forecast, so this is the representation tax alone. Bars are fraction of channel variance lost ($\mathrm  {rmse}^2$ in standardized units); the dotted line at $100\%$ is the channel's own variance, so a bar reaching it carries none of that channel and a constant would have done as well. The monthly anchor is orderly and loses most where the transport integral weights most (deep temperature, $6.9\%$). The per-bin pentad codec is near-perfect on the $92\%$ of bins that carry no Argo and collapses on the $8\%$ that do --- 40 channels competing for 32 latent dimensions. The month-block codec cures that collapse at the anchor and pays a flat structural price everywhere else: one embedding per month is a genuine $\approx $$4{:}1$ squeeze in time.}}{39}{figure.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:recon}{{15}{39}{\textbf {What each codec's round trip loses}, at full visibility --- encode and decode with nothing masked and nothing forecast, so this is the representation tax alone. Bars are fraction of channel variance lost ($\mathrm {rmse}^2$ in standardized units); the dotted line at $100\%$ is the channel's own variance, so a bar reaching it carries none of that channel and a constant would have done as well. The monthly anchor is orderly and loses most where the transport integral weights most (deep temperature, $6.9\%$). The per-bin pentad codec is near-perfect on the $92\%$ of bins that carry no Argo and collapses on the $8\%$ that do --- 40 channels competing for 32 latent dimensions. The month-block codec cures that collapse at the anchor and pays a flat structural price everywhere else: one embedding per month is a genuine $\approx $$4{:}1$ squeeze in time}{figure.15}{}}
